<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d4f217c5f465> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A filing in a case against Colombian airline Avianca cited six cases that don’t exist, but a lawyer working for the plaintiff told the court ChatGPT said they were real." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8248" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d5cbc6a3c7b8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Both lawyers, who work for the firm Levidow, Levidow & Oberman, have been ordered to explain why they should not be disciplined at an 8 June hearing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2823" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d89d1a917503> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Mr. Schwartz, who has practiced law in New York for three decades, told Judge P. Kevin Castel that he had no intent to deceive the court or the airline." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2800" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d9c07d1bee74> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The court is presented with an unprecedented circumstance,\" said United States District Judge Kevin Castel." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/da7b919e1946> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2834] ...it is well known that OpenAI’s chatGPT and other generative AI models like Microsoft Corp’s Bing AI..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2834" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dab99ffe143b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2833] OpenAI states that their ChatGPT model, trained using a machine learning technique called Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF)..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dc5c564873e6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2833] OpenAI states that their ChatGPT model, trained using a machine learning technique called Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF)..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd4d5576939d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A personal injury lawyer representing a man suing an airline now faces sanctions for citing fake cases generated by ChatGPT in court documents." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd5bb6defcb2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Presiding judge Kevin Castel expressed his doubts over the authenticity of the cases the attorney presented." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2804" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/de661fe3bf5f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2833] OpenAI states that their ChatGPT model, trained using a machine learning technique called Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF)..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/deb34371706d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"6 of the submitted cases appear to be bogus judicial decisions with bogus quotes and bogus internal citations,\" Judge Castel wrote in an order demanding the man's legal team explain itself." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2823" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/df6160985d24> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"6 of the submitted cases appear to be bogus judicial decisions with bogus quotes and bogus internal citations,\" Judge P. Kevin Castel wrote in the court order." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2820" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e01b3a0ef349> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8250] said Judge Kevin Castel of the Southern District of New York in an order." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8250" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e34c3200c3f8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As the use of generative artificial intelligence has evolved within law firms, your affiant consulted the artificial intelligence website Chat GPT in order to supplement the legal research performed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2832" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e3f3f84f1a05> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2810] Lawyer Steven A. Schwartz admitted in an affidavit that he had used OpenAI’s chatbot for his research." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2810" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e54d0ee211ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The fake cases source? ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2802" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e624a9ac2d32> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "That was because ChatGPT had invented everything." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2800" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e66fe73cf27a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A lawyer who used ChatGPT to help in research for a lawsuit could be facing sanctions after it was found the artificial intelligence chatbot made up relevant court decisions to support his client’s case." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2835" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e6aca6df0b48> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2810] Lawyer Steven A. Schwartz admitted in an affidavit that he had used OpenAI’s chatbot for his research." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2810" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e9462069eb02> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The lawyer also clarified that his fellow attorney, Peter LoDuca, had \"no role\" in performing the legal research and was not informed that ChatGPT was used." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e9a35b324468> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2822] Steven Schwartz, an attorney with the New York law firm Levidow, Levidow & Oberman, was hired by Robert Mata to pursue an injury claim against Avianca Airlines." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2822" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eaa97e1f2021> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Steven A Schwartz, who has been an attorney for more than 30 years, used ChatGPT to look for similar previous cases." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2823" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ead4b5c8b3be> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“The court is presented with an unprecedented circumstance,” wrote Manhattan federal Judge P. Kevin Castel in a May 4 document, first reported by The New York Times on Saturday, calling on Schwartz and LoDucan to appear for a June 8 hearing to face possible sanctions over the eyebrow-raising filing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2809" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ebaf68dc9bb6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2810] Lawyer Steven A. Schwartz admitted in an affidavit that he had used OpenAI’s chatbot for his research." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2810" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ee7b7bbdb5d3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2833] OpenAI states that their ChatGPT model, trained using a machine learning technique called Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF)..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eed65b9038ed> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After opposing counsel pointed out the nonexistent cases, US District Judge Kevin Castel confirmed, “Six of the submitted cases appear to be bogus judicial decisions with bogus quotes and bogus internal citations,” and set up a hearing as he considers sanctions for the plaintiff’s lawyers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8248" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ef1250251471> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A US attorney faces punishment for citing fake cases ChatGPT fed him" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2804" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ef4751972bfd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The case was originally filed. It's a complaint about 'personal injuries sustained on board an Avianca flight that was traveling from El Salvador to New York on August 27, 2019'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2848" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f06f6d69f584> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2834] ...it is well known that OpenAI’s chatGPT and other generative AI models like Microsoft Corp’s Bing AI..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2834" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f13e5e0edb6a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "His source? The infamous ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f33e3bcb1142> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In his affidavit, the lawyer, Peter LoDuca, said he had \"no reason to doubt the sincerity\" of Schwartz's work." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2824" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f46a7661b8b7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After Avianca asked to dismiss the suit because the statute of limitations had expired, Mr. Schwartz prepared a 10-page brief..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2949" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f4bc0a56872a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2834] ...other generative AI models like... Alphabet Inc.’s Google Bard..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2834" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f73f3502514d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Another attorney at the same firm, Peter LoDuca, became the attorney of record on the case, and he will have to appear in front of the judge to explain just what happened." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2810" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f80d04af0efa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "He ultimately filed the legal brief citing the fictitious cases, prompting Judge Kevin Castel to haul him into court for a hearing on whether to sanction the firm over the snafu." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f832b8453579> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Schwartz had been hired by Roberto Mata, who alleged he had suffered \"crippling\" injuries on board an airliner in 2019 when a metal trolley struck his knee." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2852" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f9509ea6bd17> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The case that wasn't made up by an AI chatbot is Roberto Mata vs. Avianca." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2811" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f96427a5290d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2834] ...other generative AI models like... Alphabet Inc.’s Google Bard..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2834" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fbcae6a9520e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A lawyer used ChatGPT for legal filing. The chatbot cited nonexistent cases it just made up" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fc90027d2d2a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This came after US District Judge Kevin Castel wrote in a May 4 order: “The court is presented with an unprecedented circumstance… Six of the submitted cases appear to be bogus judicial decisions with bogus quotes and bogus internal citations.”" ;
