    airo:evidenceText "Schwartz admitted to using ChatGPT to research for the case, representing his client Roberto Mata, to sue Colombian airline Avianca for injuries sustained onboard one of its planes in 2019." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2804" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8b9dd37af82> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In New Zealand, the Office of the Privacy Commissioner has warned of the accuracy of information created by the generative AI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a99a98aaac1f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer uses ChatGPT in court and now ‘greatly regrets’ it" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2822" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aac9e6556cfa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[8250] Among the purported cases... all of which did not appear to exist to either the judge or defense, the filing said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8250" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ac1079df8cb5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer apologises after ChatGPT invents his case law" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2852" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b03f1de20bbd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer Steven A Schwartz, who was representing a client in a lawsuit against Avianca, a Colombian airline, admitted in an affidavit that he had relied on the chatbot for his research, as reported by The New York Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2847" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b0896a237a59> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In the first instance, the attorneys filed motions in a federal court in New York City that cited nine legal cases that the opposing counsel later told the judge they could not find, according to the report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2837" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b0d0aa7f4649> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer Steven A. Schwartz admitted in an affidavit that he had used OpenAI’s chatbot for his research." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8248" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b130f3a0c63f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The bot supplied several cases that looked relevant, including Varghese v China Southern Airlines Co Ltd, from 2019, before the US Court of Appeals for the Eleventh Circuit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2852" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b2c5c5c6be31> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Clerk of the United States Court of Appeals for the Eleventh Circuit, in response to the Court's inquiry, confirmed that one of the cases cited by Schwartz - the *Varghese v China South Airlines Ltd *-- is non-existent." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b368665afcaa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The situation arose as Roberto Mata sued Avianca Airlines for injuries he sustained during a flight in 2019." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2815" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b4e86a21c6f0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "US Lawyer Faces Sanctions Over Using ChatGPT-Suggested Citations In Lawsuit" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2847" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b5592be5bfc6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shocking admission from Steven Schwartz, an attorney with firm Levidow, Levidow & Oberman, came after he asked ChatGPT to find cases relevant to his client’s lawsuit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2809" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b98493ed8bf5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer Learns Not to Use ChatGPT in Legal Research After Costly Mistake" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2817" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/baaed8297935> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2810] Lawyer Steven A. Schwartz admitted in an affidavit that he had used OpenAI’s chatbot for his research." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2810" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bbd8aa8f34ec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "U.S. District Judge P. Kevin Castel, who had asked Schwartz and his law firm Levidow, Levidow & Oberman to explain why they should not be sanctioned, said he would issue a decision later." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2945" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bdf179ef2714> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "New York Lawyer Caught Using ChatGPT After Citing Cases That Don't Exist" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2826" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/be7b09327326> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Avianca's legal team and the judge assigned to this case soon realized they could not locate any of these court decisions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c00f304709f9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Here’s What Happens When Your Lawyer Uses ChatGPT" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2800" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c1d1172efd26> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The judge in the case, P. Kevin Castel, is holding a hearing on June 8 about what to do in this tangled mess, according to the New York Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c33beb247085> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ChatGPT Causes Legal Chaos After Making Up Cases To Ease Lawyer's Workload" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2834" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c8c07e3499be> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The man, identified as Roberto Mata, sued Avianca for the alleged injuries." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2845" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ca08fd6d50be> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As the use of generative artificial intelligence has evolved within law firms, your affiant consulted the artificial intelligence website ChatGPT in order to supplement the legal research performed." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2848" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cd11ab239462> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer apologizes for fake court citations from ChatGPT" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8250" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d4f62cad1d45> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Sadly, the lawyer used the AI chatbot ChatGPT, which completely invented the cases out of thin air." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d57aba7b04e5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It turned out that at least six of the cases 'appear to be bogus judicial decisions with bogus quotes and bogus internal citations,' said Judge Kevin Castel of the Southern District of New York on May 4." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d615d7bf45cb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ChatGPT cited 'bogus' cases for a New York federal court filing. The attorneys involved may face sanctions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2821" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d68e3dd229ef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The suit involved Roberto Mata suing Avianca over claims he was injured when a metal serving cart hit his knee during August 2019 flight from El Salvador to New York." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3315" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d693fc383d2c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2837] 2 attorneys may face judicial sanctions after citing cases that were made up by ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2837" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/da27cdd804cd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Court is presented with an unprecedented circumstance. A submission filed by plaintiff's counsel in opposition to a motion to dismiss is replete with citations to non-existent cases." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2832" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/defe6b7b81da> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NYC lawyer admits he used ChatGPT to file ‘bogus’ court documents" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2809" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/df6f2d51389e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The judge ordered the attorneys to provide copies of the cases they had cited without telling them that both he and the opposing counsel had determined that the cases did not exist, the report said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2837" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e077fe612e22> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The fake cases were provided by ChatGPT, according to a May 25 affidavit by lawyer Steven A. Schwartz of Levidow, Levidow & Oberman." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2840" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e3dc72f8e033> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Schwartz, his co-counsel and his law firm now must appear before the court on June 8 to face possible sanctions for the error." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2817" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e41bc5e435b1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyers suing the Colombian airline Avianca submitted a brief full of previous cases that were just _made up_ by ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2810" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e5c6f6f9cd5c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "New York Lawyer Caught Using ChatGPT After Citing Non-Existent Cases" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2846" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e652fd285c1d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer Faces Sanctions for Using Fake ChatGPT Citations" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2825" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e653ec721c36> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Roberto Mata sued airline Avianca after he was injured by a metal serving cart colliding with his knee during a flight." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e691123e8aea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Billionaire Elon Musk hinted at such a possibility when he recently called for a six-month pause on the development of AI—a pause that likely had more to do with the fact that he was racing to build his own ChatGPT competitor." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e7d33bcbc89d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ChatGPT: US lawyer admits using AI for case research" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2823" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ea6c9b9049d2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer 'Regrets' Using ChatGPT in Legal Brief, Cites Fake Cases" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2820" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ed53188d6a87> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Steven Schwartz, an attorney with Levidow, Levidow & Oberman and licensed in New York for over three decades, handled Mata’s representation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2802" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ee398bae05d8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Steven Schwartz, an attorney with Levidow, Levidow & Oberman and licensed in New York for over three decades, handled Mata’s representation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8250" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/eecf182ce741> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer admits using ChatGPT in case where client sued airline" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f0bd0c051c41> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyers have real bad day in court after citing fake cases made up by ChatGPT" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2977" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f2950ff2a3d6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2949] The judge, P. Kevin Castel of Federal District Court, also harshly criticized the lawyers’ actions, and ordered them to send a copy of his opinion to each of the actual judges whose names appeared on the fake opinions produced by ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2949" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f8180aa5dcc6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2806] attorney Steven Schwartz of the law firm Levidow, Levidow and Oberman recently turned to OpenAI’s chatbot for assistance with writing a legal brief, with predictably disastrous results." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2806" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fa94a6009e58> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The credibility of ChatGPT, an AI chatbot developed by OpenAI, has been called into question after it deceived a lawyer into believing that citations provided by the chatbot were legitimate, when in fact they were fabricated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2847" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/faf0efa97051> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lawyer cited 6 fake cases made up by ChatGPT; judge calls it “unprecedented”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2811" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe02f901b7ed> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Schwartz used ChatGPT to generate examples of cases that supported his argument that the bankruptcy of the airline company did not affect the two-year limitation period for filing the lawsuit." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2831" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fe695c78c8e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A lawyer used ChatGPT to prepare a court filing. It went horribly awry." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2812" .

