<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e3dc1cfe428> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A personal injury lawyer in New York is facing possible sanctions after he used ChatGPT to find law cases that would help his client in a lawsuit against airline Avianca." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2817" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1b1aa9f65a01> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Let Peter LoDuca, counsel for plaintiff, show cause in person at 12 noon on June 8, 2023 in Courtroom 11D, 500 Pearl Street, New York, NY, why he ought not be sanctioned pursuant to: (1) Rule 11(b)(2) & (c), Fed. R. Civ. P., (2) 28 U.S.C. § 1927, and (3) the inherent power of the Court." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2848" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2341252cfe71> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The chatbot even claims to have double-checked its sources, finding the case in legal reference databases including LexisNexis and Westlaw, per the BBC." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2824" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e8aa847ab26> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The cases cited, with names like  Martínez v. Delta Air Lines, Zicherman v. Korean Air Lines and Varghese v. China Southern Airlines, included arguments that bolstered Mata’s case." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2835" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4deb7aada667> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the New York Times, an Avianca customer named Roberto Mata was suing the airline after a serving cart injured his knee during a flight." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b63fa44b75f1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Machine learning has now demonstrated its proficiency in handling a variety of legal tasks, spanning from intricate legal research to automated document creation and analysis of complex contracts." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2829" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ec33ae0692e7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Neither Westlaw nor Lexis has the case, and the case found at 925 F.3d 1339 is A.D. v Azar, 925 F.3d 1291 (D.C. Cir 2019)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2832" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4cddb1c40212> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "For example, Sam Altman---the CEO of ChatGPT developers OpenAI---warned during a recent Senate Judiciary Committee hearing that this technology \"can go quite wrong.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2845" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/be3e1f4f0c3b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Steven A. Schwartz -- an attorney with the law firm Levidow, Levidow & Oberman who has been practicing since 1991, according to Law & Crime -- said that he \"relied on the legal opinions provided to him by a source that has revealed itself to be unreliable.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2817" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/01f1bb5c8e08> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ChatGPT was first unleashed in November, sparking excitement and alarm at its ability to generate convincingly human-like essays, poems, form letters and conversational answers to almost any question." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5d5f7bbdb1ad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI, the company behind ChatGPT, does offer a service that tries to detect when the AI chatbot has been used, but that detector reportedly has just a 20% accuracy rate." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dbefc9cfa6bf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A tool like ChatGPT could be used in real-world applications such as digital marketing, online content creation, answering customer service queries or as some users have found, even to help debug code." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

