    airo:isRiskSourceFor <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/RiskSource/3bf92a06dd75> .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1c1f21ecceb0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "There was just 1 problem: the cases — such as Miller v. United Airlines, Petersen v. Iran Air and Varghese v. China Southern Airlines — were completely made up by ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2809" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/aea1d67082c9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Schwartz, Mata's lawyer who filed the case in state court and then provided legal research once it was transferred to Manhattan federal court, said he used OpenAI's popular chatbot in order to \"supplement\" his own findings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2803" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/931b7689fdc6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The other 5 bogus cases were called Shaboon v. Egyptair, Petersen v. Iran Air, Martinez v. Delta Airlines, Estate of Durden v. KLM Royal Dutch Airlines, and Miller v. United Airlines." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2811" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bda6b9fd3cca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ChatGPT is the conversational AI system developed by OpenAI and massively backed by Microsoft." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2816" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bf343d5a7c60> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The lawyer in the case, Steven A. Schwartz, is representing a man who’s suing Avianca Airlines after a serving cart allegedly hit his knee in 2019." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2801" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/04d286b9e700> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Among the purported cases: Varghese v. China South Airlines, Martinez v. Delta Airlines, Shaboon v. EgyptAir, Petersen v. Iran Air, Miller v. United Airlines, and Estate of Durden v. KLM Royal Dutch Airlines, all of which did not appear to exist to either the judge or defense, the filing said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8250" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1529d2e96ccc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "What makes the entire case so bizarre is the fact that while it is well known that OpenAI’s chatGPT and other generative AI models like Microsoft Corp’s Bing AI and Alphabet Inc.’s Google Bard, tends to hallucinate and provide even made up facts with utmost conviction." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2834" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b47818616c63> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "OpenAI states that their ChatGPT model, trained using a machine learning technique called Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF), can simulate dialogue, answer follow-up questions, admit mistakes, challenge incorrect premises and reject inappropriate requests." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2833" .

